    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1510">

                <pb facs="0974" n="858" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg858"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.41/162.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Simpich to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Nogales</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-03-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 2, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Reported that Carranza issued orders to Villa today that further investigations
                    of Benton case should cease for present and that Villa refrain from any further
                    discussion of case with either American or British representatives.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Simpich</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
